# 中频词汇 List01
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025恋练有词
# 描述: 中频词汇List01核心词汇

abolish /əˈbɒlɪʃ/ v. 废除 The government voted to abolish the death penalty. 政府投票废除了死刑。
abundant /əˈbʌndənt/ adj. 丰富的 The region is abundant in natural resources. 该地区自然资源丰富。
accelerate /əkˈseləreɪt/ v. 加速 The government aims to accelerate economic growth. 政府旨在加速经济增长。
accommodate /əˈkɒmədeɪt/ v. 容纳；适应 The hotel can accommodate up to 500 guests. 这家酒店可容纳多达500位客人。
accumulate /əˈkjuːmjuleɪt/ v. 积累 She accumulated a wealth of experience over the years. 她多年来积累了丰富的经验。
aggravate /ˈæɡrəveɪt/ v. 加重；使恶化 Pollution aggravates the problem of global warming. 污染加剧了全球变暖的问题。
allegation /ˌæləˈɡeɪʃn/ n. 指控 The allegations of corruption were investigated. 对腐败的指控进行了调查。
ambiguous /æmˈbɪɡjuəs/ adj. 模棱两可的 The wording of the contract is ambiguous. 合同的措辞是模棱两可的。
amend /əˈmend/ v. 修正 The law was amended to include new provisions. 法律被修正以包含新条款。
analogy /əˈnælədʒi/ n. 类比 He used an analogy to explain the complex concept. 他用类比来解释这个复杂的概念。
anticipate /ænˈtɪsɪpeɪt/ v. 预期 We did not anticipate such a strong response. 我们没有预料到如此强烈的反应。
apparatus /ˌæpəˈreɪtəs/ n. 装置；机构 The laboratory is equipped with modern apparatus. 实验室配备了现代化设备。
appliance /əˈplaɪəns/ n. 电器；器具 Modern appliances make household chores easier. 现代电器使家务更容易。
apprehend /ˌæprɪˈhend/ v. 逮捕；理解 Police apprehended the suspect within hours. 警方在几小时内逮捕了嫌疑人。
articulate /ɑːˈtɪkjuleɪt/ v./adj. 清晰表达；善于表达 She was able to articulate her ideas clearly. 她能够清楚地表达自己的想法。
aspire /əˈspaɪə(r)/ v. 渴望 Many students aspire to study abroad. 许多学生渴望出国留学。
assert /əˈsɜːt/ v. 断言；主张 He asserted his innocence throughout the trial. 他在整个审判过程中都坚称自己无罪。
assumption /əˈsʌmpʃn/ n. 假设 The assumption that all students learn at the same pace is wrong. 假设所有学生以同样的速度学习是错误的。
authentic /ɔːˈθentɪk/ adj. 真正的；可靠的 This is an authentic painting from the 18th century. 这是一幅18世纪的真品画作。
autonomy /ɔːˈtɒnəmi/ n. 自治；自主权 The university values academic autonomy. 这所大学重视学术自主权。
avert /əˈvɜːt/ v. 避免；转移 Quick action averted a disaster. 快速行动避免了一场灾难。
bandwidth /ˈbændwɪdθ/ n. 带宽；精力 We don't have the bandwidth to take on more projects. 我们没有精力承担更多项目。
barrier /ˈbæriə(r)/ n. 障碍 Language can be a barrier to communication. 语言可能成为沟通的障碍。
benchmark /ˈbentʃmɑːk/ n. 基准 The company set a new benchmark for quality. 公司设定了新的质量基准。
bloom /bluːm/ v./n. 开花；繁盛 The economy began to bloom after the reforms. 改革后经济开始繁荣。
blunder /ˈblʌndə(r)/ n./v. 大错 The company made a costly blunder. 公司犯了一个代价高昂的错误。
bolster /ˈbəʊlstə(r)/ v. 支持；增强 The new data bolstered their argument. 新数据增强了他们的论点。
boom /buːm/ n./v. 繁荣；迅速发展 The tech industry experienced a boom in the 2000s. 科技行业在21世纪初经历了繁荣。
bottleneck /ˈbɒtlnek/ n. 瓶颈 Traffic congestion is a major bottleneck for the city. 交通拥堵是该城市的主要瓶颈。
breach /briːtʃ/ n./v. 违反；缺口 The company was found to have breached the contract. 公司被发现违反了合同。
